window.GLOSS={};
window.EN={"1":"Sigurd, who had subdued the kingdom of Verdane, followed the orders from Belhalla Castle","2":"and became lord of the border castle of Evans, taking Deirdre as his wife.","3":"Grannvale's subjugation of Verdane brought great turmoil to Agustria.","4":"The lords of Agustria showed a strong will to oppose Grannvale,","5":"and the wise King Imuka of Agustria, who valued peace above all,","6":"was assassinated by an unknown hand.","7":"The one who succeeded to the throne in his place was King Imuka's eldest son, Prince Chagall.","8":"Grannvale's royal army was still far away in the east, in Isaach.","9":"Chagall ordered the lords of Agustria to invade Verdane.","10":"Sigurd, guarding Evans Castle, once again found himself in the thick of battle.","11":"Lachesis, I'm going to Agusty to ask King Chagall to call off this foolish uprising.","12":"Please wait, brother! King Chagall is a man who laid hands on even his own father,","13":"Whatever you say to someone like that is pointless. Worse, even your own life would be in danger.","14":"Lachesis, don't say such reckless things. I too have heard the rumor that Lord Chagall assassinated the former king.","15":"But there's no proof of it. If I keep trying to persuade him without giving up, I believe the king will surely understand.","16":"But...","17":"Say nothing more.","18":"In case the worst happens, I'll leave the three retainers I trust most behind at this castle.","19":"Lachesis, don't make such a sad face. It'll be fine—I'll definitely come back. I won't die and leave you behind.","20":"Brother Elt...","21":"Your Majesty Chagall, please call off this uprising.","22":"Your father wished for coexistence with Grannvale.","23":"War will only make the people suffer, and it will tarnish even your own name, Majesty.","24":"War is the one thing you must not wage!!","25":"Eldigan of Nodion, is it. You, taking advantage of being doted on by my father, have defied me endlessly until now.","26":"But... Father is dead, and now I am the ruler of all Agustria.","27":"I'll make you pay in full for all the times you made a fool of me. Someone, throw this man in the dungeon!","28":"W-wait, please! Lord Chagall...!!","29":"Heh, that Eldigan, what an eyesore. Right, order Bordeaux of Heirhein to conquer Nodion.","30":"Once that's done, we'll march on Grannvale with our full forces.","31":"...Lord Chagall, you've finally made up your mind.","32":"Manfroy, is it. Just as you said, I assassinated my father with my own hands.","33":"There's no turning back now. But can we really win?","34":"Grannvale, trusting the non-aggression pact with Agustria, has sent its entire army on campaign to Isaach.","35":"If we attack now, we will surely win.","36":"Mm, I see. If we can just defeat Grannvale, Agustria can become the ruler of the world.","37":"And then, I could become emperor.","38":"Fo fo fo... Do dream of such a thing happening...","39":"Lady Lachesis! There's a report that King Eldigan has been captured in Agusty!","40":"What, brother!? Ahh... that's why I tried so hard to stop him...","41":"Princess, that's not the only worry. We should be wary of our neighbor, Heirhein.","42":"If they learn the king is absent, they might attack at any time.","43":"They likely still hold a grudge over the fighting in Verdane, especially Prince Elliot...","44":"Elliot is angry because I won't do as he says.","45":"But I absolutely hate a conceited man like that! I couldn't fall for anyone unless he's like my brother Elt.","46":"That's why I won't become anyone's wife...","47":"...That's all well and good, but the King's own Cross Knights are currently stationed at Silesse Fort to the north,","48":"and only a small number of soldiers remain at this castle.","49":"My two younger brothers and I will protect you with all our strength, but please be prepared, just in case.","50":"I understand, Eve. I'm grateful to you. But please don't push yourself too hard—you mustn't die.","51":"Eva, please tell Alva too that Lachesis is sorry.","52":"Those words are more than we deserve.","53":"...However, we were specially chosen by King Elt and entrusted with protecting you, Princess.","54":"We too are glorious Holy Knights of Nodion. We will protect you to the very end, even at the cost of this life!","55":"What? That Eldigan incurred His Majesty's wrath and was thrown into the dungeon!?","56":"Good! Elliot! Take this chance to conquer Nodion. Make Eldigan cry out in defeat!","57":"Understood, Father.","58":"Lord Sigurd, it's terrible! Lord Eldigan has been imprisoned in Agusty Castle, and Nodion is under attack!","59":"A letter has arrived from Princess Lachesis requesting reinforcements.","60":"Eldigan!? Why—a man like him...","61":"Understood. In any case, let's march out to Nodion.","62":"I must protect Lachesis at the very least, even at the cost of my own life.","63":"Eldigan never said it aloud, but he has always cherished that princess.","64":"If he were to lose Lachesis, how deeply he would grieve...","65":"Lord Sigurd, is another battle beginning?","66":"Deirdre, I'm sorry, but I owe Eldigan a great deal.","67":"I cannot abandon his sister while she's in such distress.","68":"Yes, I understand. I won't stop you. But I'm coming with you too.","69":"What, that's no good. I don't want to put you in danger.","70":"Lord Sigurd, you promised me you'd never let me go. I... I'm anxious...","71":"...If I were apart from you, I feel like we might never meet again... Please, let me stay by your side...","72":"I'm sorry... that's right, I did promise. All right, let's go together. But you mustn't leave my side.","73":"Yes! Lord Sigurd.","74":"Princess Lachesis of Nodion, is it—that insolent woman.","75":"She's always humiliated me, but... just watch this time.","76":"Surrounded by an army this large, even Lachesis can't refuse.","77":"I'll take her back to Heirhein and make her mine, even by force.","78":"Our duty is to defend the castle, understood! Don't be distracted by the enemy in front of you—hold your position to the death!","79":"I see, so Heirhein has finally raised its army.","80":"Good, as planned—have the bandits we hired raid the village.","81":"Under the former king we couldn't lay a hand on it, but with Lord Chagall, it's easy to get away with.","82":"Seize every last bit of the village's wealth and bring it back to the castle!","83":"Heirhein is going to attack Nodion? Hmm... which side would it profit me to take...","84":"It won't be too late to wait and see how it's settled. Don't move a single soldier—let's just watch for now.","85":"...To think you've defeated me, who has never once lost before... Just who are you?","86":"There was real spirit in the way you fought. You're probably fighting for something you believe in.","87":"Until now I've only fought for money... but seeing you, that's started to feel empty.","88":"If you'll have me, I want to fight alongside you too. I want to use this sword for some greater purpose.","89":"Lady Deirdre, are you unhurt? My brother was very worried about you.","90":"Lady Ethlyn... thank you. I'm fine.","91":"I'm just happy to be able to be with Lord Sigurd.","92":"My brother is lucky to be loved by someone as kind as you.","93":"Lady Ethlyn, there's something I'd like to give you. Please take this.","94":"Huh... oh, this is the Sword of Light!? You're giving me something this important?","95":"Yes, I think it'll be of some use to you.","96":"Thank you, Lady Deirdre! I'll treasure it!","97":"Lord Sigurd! You've come to help us. Thank goodness—for a moment I didn't know what would happen...","98":"Lachesis, I'm glad you're safe. Is Eldigan still being held captive!?","99":"Yes, my brother is still in Agusty... All the lords of Agustria have become our enemies.","100":"Lord Sigurd, please lend me your strength.","101":"I must rescue my brother, no matter what...!","102":"I understand. I'm reluctant to bring my army into another nation, but this time it can't be helped.","103":"I've already obtained permission from the King of Grannvale. Prince Chagall assassinated his own father, King Imuka,","104":"and the king already knew the information that he was planning to attack Grannvale.","105":"The king declared that rescuing Eldigan, a man of peace, was also necessary for Grannvale,","106":"and entrusted me with that duty. Lachesis, I will definitely rescue Eldigan... don't worry.","107":"[Only if both Dew and Lachesis have no sweetheart]","108":"Lachesis, I've been looking for you. I found an interesting sword, and I thought I'd give it to you.","109":"Oh my, really, what an unusual sword. I've never seen one like it...","110":"It's a thief's sword, I suppose. Use it to beat up bad guys.","111":"I'm happy, but... are you sure I should take it? Won't you use it, Dew?","112":"It's fine, don't worry about it. It wouldn't mean much even if I used it myself...","113":"Heh heh, well anyway, it's a useful sword! See ya!","114":"...Ah, I'm so lonely... I'm this tough and strong, and yet everyone makes fun of me...","115":"If only I could get a follow-up attack like Alec, I could pull my weight a bit more...","116":"Then maybe I could get a girlfriend too... *sigh*... being a man is hard.","117":"Hm? What's this old bracelet? It looks like some kind of magic bracelet—let me try putting it on.","118":"Hm... mmm...! Wh-what is this feeling!? Ohh, now even I have the power to follow up...","119":"Haah~, being alone in mountains like these, I just can't stand it.","120":"No matter how much our army's prized Shooter up ahead... hm!","121":"Someone's there!! ...Or is it just my imagination...","122":"[If fought against Lachesis]","123":"Princess Lachesis, why not just give it up already. If you become my wife, I'll spare your life at least.","124":"Don't come near me! You disgust me!! I'd rather die than become your wife!","125":"[If fought against any other unit]","126":"Ugh... why is the Grannvale army here!","127":"Since it's come to this, I'll clean you all out at once!","128":"Damn it... why is it always Eldigan...","129":"Grannvale, damn you... as long as I live, I won't let you reach Heirhein Castle!","130":"Lord Bordeaux... please forgive me...","131":"What, the Grannvale army!? Damn it... every last one of them useless!","132":"Since it's come to this, I'll be your opponent myself!","133":"Ugh... my castle...","134":"Lord Sigurd, we've finally managed to subdue Heirhein. What will we do now?","135":"Indeed, the immediate crisis has passed.","136":"But Eldigan is still being held captive in Agusty. And besides...","137":"Besides?","138":"I hear a settlers' village in the central forest is being attacked by bandits. I want to help if I can.","139":"Indeed. To show that we aren't invaders, I think it's necessary to help the people.","140":"If that's decided, let's head out right away.","141":"If we dawdle, it'll be too late!","142":"You fool! While you were busy being greedy, Heirhein was taken from us, wasn't it!","143":"How do you intend to take responsibility for this mess, Macbeth!","144":"Eeek, please forgive me, Lord Chagall!","145":"I'll have Volts's mercenary corps sortie right away.","146":"Tch, a sortie order, huh. Well, can't be helped.","147":"But there's no need for us to go charging in either. Let's wait here and watch until the fighting starts.","148":"Hey, Beowolf, what'll you do?","149":"This time I'm just not feeling it. That Macbeth guy, I don't like him. I think it's about time I found myself a different employer.","150":"Suit yourself. We mercenaries are free as we please—it doesn't matter who we serve.","151":"Comrades today, enemies tomorrow—isn't that interesting too?","152":"True enough. But I don't want to fight you—I wouldn't stand a chance.","153":"Heh, there's no one who can take me down, not in this whole wide world...","154":"Village chief, something seems like a commotion—what happened?","155":"Oh, you're the traveling bard. You should hurry and prepare to flee too—a band of bandits is coming to attack.","156":"Bandits? Won't Agustria's army protect you?","157":"This country is in a state of civil war right now—there's no time to worry about the likes of us.","158":"No, in fact, the one controlling the bandits—","159":"—there's even a rumor that it's the lord of Amphony himself.","160":"That's an awful story. All right, got it—I'll go on out and take care of them.","161":"But in exchange, make the reward a generous one.","162":"You, blowing more hot air like that—if you're going to run off, just go already.","163":"We don't have time to deal with the likes of you.","164":"Tch, no one trusts me either. Well, whatever...","165":"Hey, Levin! Where are you going, leaving me behind?","166":"Ugh, Silvia! Found me, huh.","167":"What's that about, toying with someone so much and then throwing them away once you don't need them anymore?","168":"Hey now, don't say things that make me sound so bad.","169":"We only met in this village and ate together a couple of times, that's all.","170":"You're a traveling dancer, I'm a bard—that's all our relationship was, I'd think.","171":"But you told me I was cute. I... I was happy about that...","172":"That's just a habit of mine, there's no deep meaning behind it... hey, hey... don't cry in a place like this.","173":"See, everyone's gathering around now. All right, all right, come along with me then.","174":"But it's going to get a little rough. Are you ready for that?","175":"Sure, I love rough stuff!","176":"Tch, you were just crying and now you're already laughing—you're like a little kid...","177":"Did you say something?","178":"Nothing! All right, let's go!","179":"All right, this is it—men, don't give an inch! Show them the power of the mercenary corps!!","180":"Oh, that's Agusty Castle. Hey, everyone, let's take a break.","181":"If we go to the town, we might be able to hear some news about Prince Levin.","182":"Finn, this battle is against Agustrian knights—it's different from the barbarians we've faced until now.","183":"With the weapons we've had until now, we won't escape a hard fight—so I'll give you this lance.","184":"This is... the Brave Lance... are you sure it's all right for me to take this lance?","185":"You're not just my retainer—you're a precious knight who serves Leonster. I can't afford to lose you in this battle.","186":"This is about all I can do for you right now, but I want you to take it.","187":"Thank you very much, Lord Quan.","188":"You're Levin? I hear you helped the villagers. Thank you, I'm grateful.","189":"I heard you're a traveling bard, but it's surprising that you can use magic.","190":"Well, magic is part of my act too, I guess. Hmm, so you're Lord Sigurd.","191":"Going out of your way to barge into another country and wage war—you must have a lot of free time.","192":"You seem to be angry.","193":"Of course I am. Try putting yourself in the shoes of someone who actually has to work for a living.","194":"Go ahead and fight your battles if you want, but it's a nuisance for the rest of us!","195":"I'm sorry, you're quite right. I do feel bad for the people of this country.","196":"Anyone can say anything with just words. If you really think it's bad, why not go home right now?","197":"You're right... all right, I'll talk it over with everyone.","198":"Hey now, are you serious?","199":"Of course. I've been thinking about it all along—being told by you finally made up my mind.","200":"I'll stop the war. I'll try talking it over with King Chagall.","201":"It's no use saying anything to that man.","202":"If Grannvale withdraws its troops, he'll probably execute every single resident who cooperated with you, one after another.","203":"Are you really fine with that?","204":"That's... but...","205":"Hahaha, it's fine, forget it. Just as I thought, you're the kind of person I expected. I'll lend you my help too.","206":"Huh? Just who exactly are you...","207":"I'm just a traveler... a bard.","208":"Thank you for saving us. As thanks, I'll give you something precious to me.","209":"See, isn't it a beautiful bracelet? If you wear this, the shopkeepers will give you discounts.","210":"King Eldigan is too earnest for his own good. That's why he got captured by the likes of King Chagall...","211":"Please, I beg you—please save Lord Eldigan.","212":"The former king of Agustria was a fine man. But he suddenly passed away, and we're left at a loss.","213":"If his only heir is that Prince Chagall, this country won't last much longer.","214":"If it were possible, I'd want Lord Eldigan to become king...","215":"Be careful of the lord of Mackily, Father Clement.","216":"That man has a magic holy staff called the Sleep Staff.","217":"If you carelessly get close, you'll be put to sleep and rendered unable to move.","218":"Is it true that the bloodline of the dark god Loptous is still alive?","219":"In big towns like Agusty and Mackily, every year many people","220":"are burned at the stake and killed in the name of a \"demon hunt,\" even though they're not criminals—it's an awful thing.","221":"Macbeth, the lord of Amphony, is a man obsessed with money—he's tormented us terribly until now.","222":"A guy like that ought to just die!","223":"Hey, you, what do you think?","224":"King Eldigan of Nodion and his sister Princess Lachesis—don't you think they're a little too close for siblings?","225":"We're always gossiping about it. What, you think we have too much free time on our hands? Well, excuse us!!","226":"War is such a terrible thing. It's always women and children who end up crying. You should hurry back to your sweetheart too.","227":"Ohh~, well, you've come a long way. As a reward, I'll give you this sword.","228":"This is called the Armorslayer—a mysterious sword that can cut through even hard armor.","229":"If you can't use it yourself, you could sell it to a secondhand shop—it'll fetch a good price.","230":"King Eldigan of Nodion is a descendant of Hezul the Brave, one of the legendary Twelve Crusaders.","231":"The magic sword he carries, Mystletainn, together with Tyrfing of Sylvail and Balmung of Isaach,","232":"are the strongest swords in the world.","233":"I bear you no grudge, but... this is all for the sake of survival too.","234":"Ugh... no luck today...!","235":"[If holding 10,000 gold or more]","236":"You want to hire me? Then hand over 10,000 gold.","237":"...All right, I've certainly received it. I'll work at least as much as what I've been paid.","238":"[If holding less than 10,000 gold]","239":"If you want to hire me, hand over 10,000 gold. If you don't have the money, there's nothing to talk about.","240":"[If fought against Beowolf]","241":"Heh, Beowolf, is it. Seems you were a little too early to fight me.","242":"Yeah, true enough... but I'm a mercenary too. Since I've been ordered to, there's nothing for it...","243":"[If fought against any other unit]","244":"This is work too. Don't take it personally.","245":"I-impossible... to think there'd be someone who could defeat me...","246":"[If fought against Levin]","247":"W-what are you...","248":"So you're Macbeth? You seem unfit to be a lord. Give it up...","249":"[If fought against any other unit]","250":"I-impossible, Grannvale!? Damn it, those mercenaries—do they know how much I've paid them!","251":"Ugh... since it's come to this, I'll be your opponent!","252":"Guh... why me...","253":"Lord Sigurd, Lord Filat has come from Belhalla.","254":"Lord Filat, welcome. Thank you for coming.","255":"Lord Sigurd, so it has finally become full-scale war with Agustria. How goes the fighting?","256":"We're managing to fight, but it's been difficult.","257":"By the way, Lord Sigurd, this is hard to bring up, but...","258":"Yes, what is it?","259":"There are unpleasant rumors about you within the royal court.","260":"That you've joined forces with Prince Quan of Leonster and King Eldigan of Nodion, and are plotting rebellion against the king.","261":"And that for that purpose, you're even harboring the prince of Isaach...","262":"What, that's absurd! Just who would say such a thing...","263":"It's Duke Reptor and Lord Langobalt.","264":"I see... those two hate my father, so... but even so, that's a terrible thing to say...","265":"Those two are jealous that Prince Kurth relies solely on Lord Byron.","266":"If the prince becomes king, those two would certainly lose their positions. They're probably anxious about that.","267":"In any case, you'd do well to be cautious.","268":"Understood. By the way, Lord Filat, has the war with Isaach still not ended?","269":"According to reports, it seems mostly settled. Your father should be returning in triumph along with Prince Kurth before long, together.","270":"I'm relieved Prince Kurth is safe too. Since he still has no wife,","271":"my father was always worried that if anything happened to him, the royal bloodline would die out.","272":"Indeed, we too keep telling him he should take a wife soon, but...","273":"Is there some reason for it?","274":"Hmm... this is something only a few people even at court know, but...","275":"The prince once deeply loved a certain woman in the past, and it's said he still hasn't been able to forget her.","276":"Why weren't they able to be together?","277":"Well... I'll tell you everything. It happened about twenty years ago.","278":"The prince fell in love with Duke Vertomer's beautiful wife—that is to say, a woman who was already another man's wife.","279":"Duke Vertomer was a man of poor character with women, and had many mistresses. Since the prince was an earnest man,","280":"he probably felt sympathy for her at first, but before long, the two of them came to deeply love each other...","281":"But Duke Vertomer, driven into a fury, left behind a letter cursing the two of them and took his own life,","282":"and as a result, the lady too could no longer bear to stay and disappeared. Her name was, I believe... Sigyun, I think it was.","283":"...Such a thing happened... then, Lord Arvis's mother was...","284":"That's right. Lord Arvis was about seven years old, I believe. Losing both parents at once—it was pitiable.","285":"I see... but the prince is just as pitiable, isn't he. And that lady too...","286":"No, I've gone and told you something trivial. Court gossip is of no use to a warrior like yourself.","287":"Please forget it. The war with Agustria will surely continue for some time yet.","288":"I look forward to the day you return in triumph to your homeland.","289":"What, even Amphony has been subdued... hmm... so they intend to conquer all of Agustria, do they.","290":"Since it's come to this, there's no choice but to fight. Get the Shooter into position.","291":"We mustn't let the Grannvale army reach Agusty!","292":"King Chagall, how much longer must we wait?","293":"We must find Prince Levin as soon as possible.","294":"We're staying in this castle because you said you knew where the prince was.","295":"Ah, forgive me. But, I've finally found out.","296":"Prince Levin is being held captive by the Grannvale army. They're invading our country,","297":"and on top of that, it seems they're indiscriminately capturing and executing even unrelated people.","298":"The prince too has been captured at their base, Evans, and it's said he'll be executed soon. You must hurry to save him, or it'll be dangerous.","299":"W-what a thing... understood, I'll head to Evans at once and rescue the prince.","300":"Queen Lahna of Silesse told me to avoid conflict with other nations, but it can't be helped.","301":"I'll attack the Grannvale army the moment I find them.","302":"Oh, that's exactly what I hoped for. I leave it in your hands.","303":"Then, if you'll excuse me.","304":"Heh, she's gone, has she... foolish woman... all right, send out the knights from Agusty too! Let's settle this in one blow!!","305":"Eek, it's Lord Sigurd!!","306":"Huh? You're the dancer? This is a battlefield, it's dangerous—go back to the castle.","307":"Lord Sigurd, don't you know who I am? I'm Silviaaa. You can call me Silvy if you like.","308":"...I'm sorry, but I don't have time to deal with a child. Be a good girl and go home.","309":"Hmph... you think this sexy me is a child?","310":"Lord Sigurd might actually be a surprisingly boring man...","311":"Hey now, I can hear you.","312":"Oh well, fine. I'm a flower blooming on the battlefield—when it's time to fall, I'll fall in a blaze of glory.","313":"What am I going to do with this girl...","314":"[Only if both Alec and Silvia have no sweetheart]","315":"Oh, so you're Silvia. Hmm, nice, you're cute.","316":"Oh wow, I thought everyone here was a stiff, but there's a normal guy after all.","317":"That's right, I'm probably the only normal one. I really like girls like you.","318":"Thanks.","319":"When I've got some free time, I'd like to talk with you properly. Is that all right?","320":"Sure, I'll show you my dancing too.","321":"A special one I haven't shown anyone else—it's a little embarrassing, but I'll show it to you.","322":"I-is that so... I'll look forward to it...","323":"[Only if both Beowolf and Lachesis have no sweetheart]","324":"Huh, so you're the princess of Nodion.","325":"How rude. Who are you!","326":"Oh, sorry about that. I'm Beowolf, just a lowly mercenary.","327":"So, do you have some business with me?","328":"Yeah, there's just one thing I wanted to say—war isn't a game.","329":"Having a chick like you wandering around is a nuisance for the rest of us.","330":"If you're a princess, act like one and stay quietly in your castle.","331":"Well! I have no reason to be told that by you! That's none of your business!","332":"Heh heh, you really are Eldigan's sister—you've certainly got spirit, at least.","333":"Eh? ...You know my brother?","334":"Yeah, I've known that guy for a long time. He asked me to look out for you, that's why I'm meddling like this.","335":"Oh, is that so... I'm sorry.","336":"Well, it's fine. All right, let me teach you a bit about fighting. This is for Eldigan's sake too.","337":"Yes, please do!!","338":"[If fought against Levin]","339":"Prince Levin!? No, that can't be...","340":"[If fought against any other unit]","341":"Knight of Grannvale, return Prince Levin to us!!","342":"Ahh... Lady Lahna... please forgive me...","343":"Fury!? What are you doing in a place like this?","344":"Huh? You're... c-could it be... Prince Levin? What's happened, looking like that?!","345":"Ah, this outfit? I'm working as a traveling bard right now. What do you think, suits me, doesn't it?","346":"...But, why...","347":"...I heard the prince was being held captive in Evans and rushed here in a panic...","348":"Me, held captive in Evans? Who told you something like that?","349":"King Chagall of Agusty...","350":"Ah-hah, Fury, you've been deceived.","351":"Being honest is fine, but you can't live in the city that way.","352":"Though it'd also be a problem if you got weirdly worldly like Silvia...","353":"Prince Levin, who is Silvia...","354":"Oh, well... never mind that. Anyway, why are you here?","355":"Of course, to bring you back to Silesse, Prince.","356":"It's been nearly two years since you left the country without telling anyone, and Queen Lahna is very worried.","357":"Please come back with me.","358":"If I go back, I'll have to succeed to the throne according to the late king's will.","359":"But my uncles will never agree to it. If it goes badly, it could turn into a civil war like this country's.","360":"If that happens, the people will suffer the most. As for being king, whoever wants it badly enough can have it.","361":"I like my free life as it is now. Succeeding to the throne is the last thing I want.","362":"Something like that, I may as well just hand it over to my uncles.","363":"That won't do. The Silesse royal family is a noble house descended from the wind god Forseti,","364":"and you, Prince, are the only one who has inherited that power.","365":"There is no one else who can succeed to the Silesse throne besides you. All the people wish for it too.","366":"Prince Levin... Lady Lahna was in tears. Please... please come back.","367":"Fury... there's no need for you to cry too, is there.","368":"Give me a break—I'm weak against a woman's tears.","369":"All right, fine. But let me think about it a bit more. Once I've made up my mind, I'll return to my mother.","370":"Then, please let me stay by your side until you return, Prince.","371":"I'll have my subordinates relay that you're safe.","372":"Even if I say no, you won't listen, will you. Fine then,","373":"I'll travel with Lord Sigurd for a while. We somehow get along well, and besides, his army has a lot of beautiful women.","374":"You should make friends with them too, Fury. Maybe then you'll become a little more polished.","375":"Yes...","376":"Hey now, that was a joke. Don't take it seriously.","377":"Honestly, you're so earnest, Fury... you're cute enough that no one could beat you. You're more than fine the way you are.","378":"Y-yes... ah, I mean...","379":"Are you Lord Sigurd?","380":"Yes, I am. And you?","381":"I'm Fury, a knight of Silesse. In order to protect Prince Levin, I'll be accompanying you for a while.","382":"Prince Levin? What do you mean by that?","383":"Prince Levin is the rightful heir to the Silesse royal family,","384":"one who has inherited the power of the Wind Crusader, Lord Sety.","385":"What, that Levin!? I see... I thought there was something to him, but to think he was the prince of Silesse.","386":"But why would he become a bard, of all things...","387":"There are various circumstances, but it's not for me to say. Please leave him be for a while.","388":"Understood. I'll continue to treat him the same as before.","389":"Fury, it would be a great help if you, a Pegasus Knight, would cooperate with us. I'm counting on you.","390":"Yes, leave it to me!","391":"Damn it, you invaders!... Given how things stand, I myself will be your opponent!","392":"Guh... remember this...","393":"Good, Mackily is subdued. Next is finally the capital, Agusty.","394":"Yes, Lord Sigurd. But there's information that a large force still remains at Agusty.","395":"Please be careful.","396":"Indeed, that's true. As for Chagall, who knows what he's plotting...","397":"What, even Mackily has fallen!? Zane, this can't be helped—you lead the remaining full army and march out!","398":"Yes, but...","399":"No back-talk, hurry and go!!","400":"Chagall, you're being disgraceful. It's not as though you've already lost.","401":"You, Manfroy!","402":"Grgh... I did as you said and look where it's gotten me! What are you going to do about this!","403":"Fu fu fu, I only ever said to kill the king if he was in your way.","404":"Everything came from your own ambition, didn't it.","405":"Damn it, I never imagined Sigurd's army would be this strong...","406":"Manfroy, tell me, what on earth should I do?","407":"There's still a way.","408":"If it comes down to it, just make use of that brat—Eldigan, who's held in the dungeon.","409":"Even Sigurd won't be able to refuse if it comes from him.","410":"You'd best apologize to him while you still can.","411":"Y-yes, you're right. Eldigan would help us, surely. All right, I'll do that.","412":"Heh, what a fool...","413":"Archbishop Manfroy, I have confirmed the assassination of Prince Kurth.","414":"I see. Those fools move about so entertainingly for us.","415":"Of our ancient enemy, the line of Naga, only that old relic remains. It's only a matter of time before he too drops dead.","416":"After that, if we can just revive the dark god, the world will be ours...","417":"Has Lord Arvis agreed to the Archbishop's proposal?","418":"He can hardly refuse. The blood of Loptous flows in his body.","419":"If that were ever to leak out, he would be captured and burned at the stake as a member of the dark god's bloodline.","420":"Could a man as proud as him ever endure such a thing?","421":"Then, he'll betray the king and become emperor himself...","422":"Indeed... but that alone isn't enough.","423":"For the god Loptous to be reincarnated, Arvis and... one more person—that woman's daughter—is needed...","424":"Sortie! Take pride in being able to die for your homeland!","425":"Damn you, Grannvale... since it's come to this, a warrior's pride is at stake! I'll clean you all out at once!","426":"Guh... is this the end for Agustria too, then...","427":"[If fought against Fury]","428":"Heh heh heh, so it's you... seems you've finally realized it, you foolish woman!","429":"Chagall! How dare you deceive me! I won't forgive you, of all people—prepare yourself!!","430":"[If fought against Lachesis]","431":"Grgh, you're Eldigan's sister. What do you think you're doing, defying me?","432":"I don't consider you a king at all! Return my brother to me at once!!","433":"[If fought against any other unit]","434":"Tch... don't underestimate me. There's no way the likes of you could defeat me.","435":"Ugh... w-wait... just spare my life, at least...","436":"[Only if Deirdre has lost a battle even once]","437":"Deirdre!? Thank goodness, you're safe!","438":"Yes, I was captured by the enemy and brought to this castle... I believed you'd surely come to save me.","439":"[Only if Lachesis, Eve, Eva, and Alva are all alive]","440":"Lady Lachesis, we're returning to Nodion, but there's something we'd like to give you, Princess.","441":"This is called the Knight Ring—a magic bracelet that lets even non-knights move again.","442":"I'm sure it will be of use to you, Princess. Well then, please take care!","443":"Lord Sigurd, King Chagall is gravely wounded, but it seems he's still alive. It's said the palace priests are tending to him.","444":"I heard someone rescued King Chagall from the battlefield. I wonder who on earth it was.","445":"It was me, Sigurd... I rescued the king. He's the only member of the Agusty royal family left.","446":"No matter what kind of man he is, he's still my liege lord without question. I couldn't let him die.","447":"Ah, Eldigan!? You're safe!","448":"Thank goodness. I heard you'd been captured, so I was looking for you.","449":"Yes, somehow I'm all right. But Sigurd, what is the meaning of this?","450":"The capital Agusty has been subdued by your army,","451":"and from what I hear, officials have been dispatched from Grannvale to castles everywhere, treating this as if it were a subject nation.","452":"Has Agustria been occupied by Grannvale without my knowledge?","453":"Sigurd, depending on your answer, I won't go easy on you either, even you!","454":"I'm sorry, Eldigan. I'm not entirely satisfied with that matter myself either.","455":"But the king said that, aside from you, the fact remains that the lords of Agustria turned hostile against our nation,","456":"and for the sake of maintaining order, he ordered me to remain in this land for a while.","457":"Eldigan, please, just wait one year.","458":"With a year, peace should be restored and relations with Agustria mended too.","459":"Once that happens, we'll return to our country. The king promised me as much.","460":"I see... if you say so much, I have no choice but to trust you. All right... one year, then.","461":"Good. Until then, I'll guard King Chagall at Madino Castle to the north.","462":"My Cross Knights happen to be stationed at Silesse Fort too,","463":"and if it comes to it, I could crush the Grannvale army at any time.","464":"If you break your promise, then I'll fight you for real too! You understand that, don't you, Sigurd!","465":"Of course. I won't betray you. Trust me, Eldigan."};
